      "Her unconventional early education was further enriched by her godfather Timothy Leary's extensive personal library and family friendships with visionary science fiction authors Philip K. Dick and Aldous Huxley's inner circle. This rich intellectual immersion instilled a profound skepticism toward commercial conformity, encouraging her to seek out unconventional, psychologically challenging screenplays that other young Hollywood contemporaries routinely avoided."
